% Loaded by Documenter's LaTeX preamble, which already puts the title,
% the version and the authors on the cover page and a table of contents
% after it. This file adds the one thing REQ-304 asks for and Documenter
% does not supply: the licence, at the foot of the cover page.
%
% `memoir` calls \maketitlehooka ... \maketitlehookd from inside
% \maketitle; hook d runs last, so the notice lands under the author.
% \providecommand first, in case a future memoir drops the hook.
%
% The string below is checked against the first line of LICENSE.md at
% build time by docs/make_pdf.jl: if the two ever disagree, the build
% fails rather than print a licence the repository does not carry.
\providecommand{\DocLicence}{BSD 3-Clause License}
\providecommand{\maketitlehookd}{}
\renewcommand{\maketitlehookd}{%
  \vfill
  \begin{center}
    \small
    Licensed under the \DocLicence.\\
    Generated from the package sources with Documenter.jl
    on Julia \JuliaVersion.\\
    This document describes an implementation of the methodology of
    JCGM 100:2008.\\
    It is not accredited calibration software; see the Limitations
    chapter.
  \end{center}
}
